$WSROOT/large/s2/sol-query8w-r0/step3/NOTES.md
diff --git a/NOTES.md b/NOTES.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..a2a24ad3a71c974a28e4da0f497c9960ef87a3ee
--- /dev/null
+++ b/NOTES.md
@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@
+Inferred earlier corrections: (1) Escalation should depend on operational severity, not anger alone. (2) EU alerts receive increased escalation preference, but low-severity EU alerts can remain suppressed. These are qualitative inferences from the earlier evidence; the examples do not uniquely identify their formulas. I preserve the existing model computation.
+
+New correction: Force escalation when tier_critical = 1 and error_rate > 0.70, regardless of other features. Otherwise preserve the current decision. Query labels select C2 over C1 and C3. The 0.70/0.71 queries support the chosen strict threshold but do not uniquely locate it within that interval.
+
+Let f be the original logit. Three added channels compute a = ReLU(error_rate - 0.70), b = ReLU(0.70 - error_rate), and n = 1 - tier_critical. The final layers return ReLU(f - a + b + n) + a - b - n = max(f, a - b - n). This implements the required decision everywhere on the stated domain. All original weights and biases remain in the computation. No training or fitting occurred.
+
+Preservation applies to decisions; logit values can change. Exact exterior logit preservation is incompatible with continuity at a negative-logit override boundary.
+
+Validation: 118/118 supplied labels, 50,000 random decisions, and 12,000 boundary decisions passed.

